      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-16T22:46:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Using withTimeout, you will have to catch the exception to handle it as desired, so I used withTimeoutOrull, which doesn\u0027t throw an exception and returns null on timeout.\n\nI used withTimeoutOrNull here specifically so that I can cleanup (cancel the scope so that BT state change broadcasts are unregistered) before doing any asserts that will end the test.",
      "parentUuid": "86858f67_1afac766",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 281,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 281,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "800fca855b5601bbc7ea7df89096a127db720242",
