      "writtenOn": "2024-01-17T01:09:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "bluetoothStateFlow.map { it \u003d\u003d BluetoothAdapter.STATE_OFF }.first { it }\n-\u003e Converts the BT state to a Boolean and returns the first Boolean that\u0027s true.\n\nbluetoothStateFlow.first { it \u003d\u003d BluetoothAdapter.STATE_OFF }\n-\u003e Emits the first BT state that matches the predicate\n\nSo, one\u0027s returning Boolean and the other returning BT state. Anyways, now that I have refactored to use withTimeout to let timeout exception be sent downstream, I don\u0027t need to use map. Updated accordingly.",
      "parentUuid": "42f79059_a8b7076e",
